  "omissions": [
    {
      "tib": "de'i",
      "reason": "Its anaphoric textual reference is expanded as in the text; later on is attached only to 'og tu."
    },
    {
      "tib": "gyi bdag nyid yin",
      "reason": "part of the mind itself distributes the nature/identity expression; mind and only are independently sound, but neither part nor itself alone is asserted as the complete bdag nyid equivalent. Omitted, not nulled."
    },
    {
      "tib": "zhes de",
      "reason": "The citation/exposition is rendered with Master Vinitadeva says and He is saying that; de is then expanded as pus and blood. These English participant/explanatory repetitions remain unwrapped."
    },
    {
      "english": "second if; provide; nonetheless; his point; by using",
      "reason": "Repeated conditional/concessive marking or explanatory light/support wording beyond the claimed atoms; remains verbatim unwrapped."
    },
    {
      "tib": "other case/copular/nominal endings",
      "reason": "Unclaimed grammar; no blanket null assertion."
    }
  ],
  "contentious_decisions": [
    "HGM master explicitly records bya byed → actions and their objects, bza' btung → something to eat or drink, mi nus → could never, gnod pa → injury, and der thal → this is certainly the case. The first two are retained as complete lexical compounds without speculative members.",
    "C15:436 has identical ACIP and Wylie, with English punctuation differences around the first conditional. Its whole quoted verse and continuation support exactly their shared text, not byte identity of full English.",
    "The second not/exist pair is the concessive explanation after the quotation; it must not attach to the first conditional. Examples and the final dream belong to the proof, not the quoted analogy."
  ]
